'''Prof. Owlbrowley''' (ふくろう博士, ''Fukurō-hakase'', '''Professor Owl''') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Owlbrow]] that appears in [[Zero Legends]]. They were added in [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Prof. Owlbrowley
|image = E 713.png
|first appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Incompetent Watchman|Sub-chapter 17 - Incompetent Watchman]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Marble Swamp|Sub-chapter 18 - Marble Swamp]]
|money drop = 1,000¢ - 3,950¢
}}

==Enemy==
Prof. Owlbrowley has much higher health, damage and speed than [[Owlbrow]], but retains the same role as a relatively frail yet hard-hitting midranger, with a guaranteed 4-second freeze making their attacks even deadlier. Their standing range is increased to 360, and an [[Othom]]-esque Omni Strike extends their reach to 440. Unlike Owlbrow, Prof. Owlbrowley has a brief idle animation which extends their attack cycle to 4.77s, keeping their freeze uptime just short of 100%.

==Strategy==
Though Prof. Owlbrowley does 42,000 damage every hit at 100% magnification with 80 piercing range, their attack cycle is even longer, allowing fast units like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to rush in and cripple or outright remove them, as their health still isn't too high. A level 50 Fishman Cat with 3 (+) levels or a level 3 Attack Buff Talent is capable of killing a 100% Prof. Owlbrowley in just two hits, making it one of the best units for taking them out quickly.

